      ":question/id": "393441ef-e82e-58c7-96cf-0bd35884528c",
      ":question/problem": "If $A$ is a $10\\times 12$ matrix that has $5$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\text{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ \n\nSince $A$ has $12$ columns and $5$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n12-5=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(A)=7.$",
